  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "IMCSCH forms the scaled reciprocal of IMSINH(z) without EXP's real-axis overflow check, returning \"0\" at 1e100",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMCSCH(inumber) computes sinh(inumber) through hyperbolic_parts (with 0.01 Taylor and 20.0 EXP(|x|)/2 cutoffs) without IMSINH's real-axis EXP-overflow #NUM! check, then takes the single scaled reciprocal 1 / sinh(z) with subnormals flushed to 0. Consequently IMCSCH(0) returns #NUM! while IMCSCH(1e100) returns \"0\". All 1,279 full-bank IMCSCH rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence cache/w111-extended-regenerated-20260929/answers-imcsch.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (prefix_metadata row 119); 1,279/1,279 full-bank rows match.",
